## Findings (measurements, not axis verdicts)

- F-1 (battery 4a falsifier fired — leg-order premise inverted): the battery
  predicted glm-flash-cascade prompt_tokens 11734 [10000,13000] on the
  premise "first leg devin" (r18 census D9/M3 era). The live shim is
  zai-first (M9 reorder, unit Description zai -> devin -> hyper, journal
  leg=1/zai), and the observed 407 came from the DEVIN leg serving after a
  zai 429 — the devin leg billed 407 for the identical prompt that
  [M9] measured at 140-396 and [CENSUS D9] at 11734. The 11734-era figure
  belongs to the pre-M9 devin-first cascade; under the current order the
  devin leg is a FALLBACK and bills ~400. The battery's 4a/4c premises are
  stale in both directions (order changed AND fallback billing is small).
- F-2 (defect, serving plane, unowned — route per PROVINCE §Refusals): the
  devin leg (devin-openai-shim/2) rejects any body carrying `temperature`
  with 400 devin_shim_error/invalid_argument, and the glm cascade treats
  that 400 as TERMINAL (no data_inspection_failed marker ⇒ no fall-through,
  [CODE] :253-267), so a zai 429 + a temperature-bearing body = caller gets
  400 with zero glm output. Any client sending OpenAI-standard temperature
  through this cascade during a zai 429 window loses the call. Receipts:
  attempt 1 (this log §1) + the direct-8787 cross-check. Owner: unowned
  serving plane (PROVINCE.md:24-25); reported to the integrator, not fixed.
- F-3 (zai leg rate-limit state): journal since the patched restart
  (2026-10-15 14:16:30 -03 → 04:53:22 -03 window read at 07:54Z): zai leg
  302 OK / 547 FAIL-429 (35.6% serve) in one burst window 04:36-04:53 local;
  per-minute OK 7-24 during the window; the shim absorbed every fallthrough
  (devin 525 OK / 0 FAIL in the same read). The operator's zai-first policy
  is currently serving ~36% of glm-flash traffic directly; the rest pays the
  devin fallback. This is a route-state measurement, not a model-quality
  signal (ledger-route-telemetry.md:60-62 frame).
- F-4 (incidental, zero-content at 16 tokens): the scored run produced 0
  content tokens (finish_reason=length, 16 reasoning tokens) — consistent
  with the r18 digest's no-content behaviour class on glm flash lanes and
  with runner-leg-opencode's incidental observation (their log §Request 2).

